// For a machine you watch from somewhere else: your work, and a controller.
//
//   zellij -n agenttij-remote          on the dev box
//
// There is no sidebar here on purpose. A sidebar is a column you look at, and you
// are not looking at this machine — you are looking at it through the sidebar on
// the one in front of you. What this layout adds instead is a *controller*: the
// same plugin with `remote "true"`, which draws nothing, takes no keys, and does
// three things.
//
//   - keeps this session to one pane of a row at a time, with real suppressed
//     panes, the way `solo "true"` does at home
//   - publishes its rows to /tmp/agenttij/rows, which a sidebar elsewhere reads
//     over ssh along with the state files
//   - does what that sidebar asks: `zellij -s <session> pipe --name add`, or
//     cycle, show, close
//
// It is declared *floating*, which is what keeps it off the screen: Zellij shows
// floating panes only while one of them holds focus, and this one is unselectable
// so it never can. `hide_self` looks like the obvious way to do that and was
// measured not removing a plugin pane from the layout.
//
// It also has to be here rather than launched on demand: `zellij action
// launch-plugin` is refused for a session with nobody attached ("No connected
// clients found"), and a session waiting for you to arrive has nobody attached.
layout {
    pane
    pane

    floating_panes {
        pane {
            plugin location="file:~/.config/zellij/plugins/agenttij.wasm" {
                remote "true"
            }
        }
    }
}
